    {"@id":"source:caid","@type":["Source","EmpiricalStudy"],"name":"Effective Strategies for Asynchronous Software Engineering Agents","summary":"CAID study combining centralized dependency-aware planning, asynchronous isolated execution, structured integration, and executable verification. Cited at arXiv:2603.21489v2 (8 Jul 2026), retrieved 2026-08-30 (first retrieved 2026-08-29): v2 reports +25.6 absolute on PaperBench and +14.7 on Commit0 versus single-agent baselines. The superseded arXiv:2603.21489v1 (23 Mar 2026) reported +26.7 and +14.3; see sourcerev:caid-v1 and sourcerev:caid-v2. CAID's within-paper comparison is worktree isolation against soft isolation (v2 Table 3), not snapshot against rebase and not coordination against isolation.","status":"preprint","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.21489v2","source_kind":"paper","authors":"CAID authors (see arXiv listing)","year":2026,"venue_or_publisher":"arXiv","identifier":"arXiv:2603.21489v2","retrieved_at":"2026-08-30","relations":[{"predicate":"hasRevision","target":"sourcerev:caid-v1"},{"predicate":"hasRevision","target":"sourcerev:caid-v2"},{"predicate":"uses","target":"source:paperbench-2025"},{"predicate":"uses","target":"source:commit0-2024"}],"verification":[]},
